      "writtenOn": "2018-05-16T07:07:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not convinced doing a loop here polling forever is right.\n\nWhile Fizz added a similar system, it was only for the battery-less chromebox.\n\nFrom a high-level PoV, going to S5 doesn\u0027t require 7.5W, does it ?\n(S3/S0 might certainly)\n\nFrom an implementation perspective, it\u0027s weird to spin here in a \u0027transition\u0027 state (G3S5),\nwhy it is exiting G3 in first place if you don\u0027t want ?\nwhy the waiting for this condition is not handled by the regular state machine ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 578,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 580,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "27a75060d8405380ae2611def93bfcb0bb0e6114",
